{
  "manufacturer": "Teracom",
  "manufacturer_slug": "teracom",
  "model": "TST320 2-channel thermocouple module with Modbus RTU",
  "model_slug": "tst320",
  "short_model": "TST320",
  "aliases": [
    "TST320"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Sensor (thermocouple input module)",
  "applies_to": "TST320 per the Teracom TST320 user manual Revision R1.6.",
  "summary": "The TST320 is a DIN-rail Teracom module that reads two thermocouples (J, K, T, N, E, B, R, S) and serves them over Modbus RTU RS-485. It gives current, minimum and maximum temperatures in Â°C and Â°F as floats and scaled integers, with per-channel type, multiplier and offset.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 19200,
    "parity": "Even",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "The register table prints both a PDU (wire) address and a logical address (PDU + 40001 for holding registers). 'documented' holds the logical number; the PDU number is what goes in the request, e.g. logical 40101 = PDU 100."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "TST320 User manual",
    "doc_number": "Revision R1.6",
    "revision_date": "2026-10",
    "url": "https://www.teracomsystems.com/download/tst320-2-channel-thermocouple-module-with-modbus-rtu-interface-tst320/",
    "pages": "pp. 4-5 (Modbus address table)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Addresses are taken from the manual's PDU address column (0-based); the logical column is the same number plus 40001, the holding-register offset the manual states.",
    "All 32-bit values follow the Data order register (PDU 13): 1 = most significant word first (factory default), 2 = least significant word first. The map shows the default, ABCD.",
    "Left out: the 32-bit float/integer test-value registers (PDU 82-95), which only exist to check word order; the 16-bit test values are kept.",
    "Integer formats as the table lists them: x10 values are 16-bit signed; x100 current Â°C values are 16-bit signed, while the x100 min/max Â°C and all x100 Â°F values are 32-bit signed.",
    "A missing thermocouple returns NaN (float), -32768 (16-bit) or -2147483648 (32-bit).",
    "Min/max values are cleared through PDU 1000.",
    "Left out: the current-value °C x100 registers (PDU 600 and 602). The table calls them 16-bit signed but spaces them two registers apart like the 32-bit rows around them, so their size is unclear."
  ],
